      "explanation": "Senator Cornyn is writing a letter to the DHS Secretary to urge consideration of a proposal. According to negative clarification (d), writing a letter or making an appeal where no positive response or completed outcome is yet achieved does not constitute credit-claiming."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "2869",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "Senator Jeffords is explaining his vote on amendments regarding Iraq. According to negative clarification (c), explaining a vote or taking a stance on a national controversy is not credit-claiming."
