    {
      "document_id": "714",
      "label": "1",
      "explanation": "The senator explicitly claims credit for helping to secure more than $3 billion in the fiscal year 2006 Homeland Security appropriations bill for ICE's domestic enforcement efforts, which benefits law enforcement coordination in Idaho."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "3252",
      "label": "1",
      "explanation": "Senator Nelson is claiming credit for the successful passage of his amendment to the Agriculture Appropriations bill, which prevents Japanese beef imports until Japan allows US beef imports. This meets clarification (b) for pointing to specific amendments they authored that successfully passed the Senate."
